{
  "requirement": "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is\ncheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors\nselect it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames\nwithout an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural check finds no gap in `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.language`. I did not assess runtime behavior, and I did not look for tests.\n\n- **Trait implementation:** The `language!(PlainText, super::plain::PROFILE, \"plain-text-structural-v1\")` invocation in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs` carries the `{impl}` reference. It expands to `pub struct PlainText;` and `impl OutlineLang for PlainText`. That impl defines `name`, `extensions` and `outline`, matching the signatures in `requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. `name` and `extensions` read from the profile.\n- **Default value:** The macro derives `Clone, Copy, Debug, Default`. `PlainText` is a unit struct, so cloning copies nothing and no prepared configuration is rebuilt. This covers \"default value is cheaply cloneable\".\n- **No claimed extensions:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/plain.rs#static[PROFILE]` sets `extensions: &[]` and `language: None`. The `OutlineLang::extensions` implementation returns that empty slice.\n- **Filename-based selection:** `OutlineContent::from_source` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs` first calls `languages::registry().for_path(filename)`. If that returns no provider, it falls back to `from_source_with(&languages::PlainText, ...)`. `Registry::for_path` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/language.rs` uses `path.extension()?`, so a filename with no extension returns `None` and also reaches plain text. `profile_for_path` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/profile.rs` falls back to `plain::PROFILE` the same way.\n\nEvery structural obligation in the text is supported. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "d364693a64f673cea5b31c5d57cc4436a3d085824fd398288e275ce0c804733a",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.language",
      "matches": [
